<para id="RM000002NZF00QX" category="J" type-id="305BG" name-id="066OT-00" from="200708">
<dtccode/>
<dtcname>VC Power Source Circuit</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000002NZF00QX_01" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000EV300000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<list1 type="nonmark">
<item>
<ptxt>The engine control computer constantly generates 5V from the battery voltage applied to the +B (BATT) terminal to operate the CPU. Furthermore, the engine control computer supplies this power to the sensors through the VC output circuit.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A147816J04" width="7.106578999in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<ptxt>If the VC circuit is shorted, no power is supplied from the VC circuit, so the CPU in the engine control computer and the sensors receiving power through the VC circuit stop. In this condition, the system does not start up, and the check engine warning light does not come on even if there is a system malfunction.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>Normally, the check engine warning light comes on for a few seconds when the engine switch is first turned ON. When the engine starts, the check engine warning light goes off.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</item>
</list1>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002NZF00QX_02" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000EV400000">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A160636J05" width="7.106578999in" height="6.791605969in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002NZF00QX_03" type-id="51" category="05">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000002NZF00QX_04" type-id="01" category="01">
<name>Procedure</name>
<testgrp id="RM000002NZF00QX_04_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___0000EV500000">
<testtitle>Check that Check Engine Warning Light Comes On</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Turn the IG ON.</ptxt>
</test1>
<test1>
<ptxt>Check that the check engine warning light in the combination meter assembly comes on.</ptxt>
<spec>
<title>Result</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="3.01in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.12in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Result</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Proceed to</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Check engine warning light does not come on</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>A</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Check engine warning light comes on</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>B</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002NZF00QX_04_0002" fin="false">A</down>
<right ref="RM000002NZF00QX_04_0008" fin="true">B</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002NZF00QX_04_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___0000EV600000">
